{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>{{ page_title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">
  No single page covers every lake. These are the pages people use to check a
  California algae advisory, what each one covers and what it does not. Check
  more than one, and read the signs posted at the water.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  This page is a dated snapshot. We read each page below on
  {{ as_of|date }}, and pages change, move and go out of date without notice.
  Open the link to see what it says now. Lake Notice is independent and no
  agency or organization listed here has reviewed or approved this page.
</p>

<h2 id="table">Sources</h2>
<table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Where to check an algae advisory in California: each source, the date we read it, what it covers and what it does not</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Read on</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th><th scope="col">What it does not cover</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in sources %}
    <tr id="{{ s.slug }}">
      <td>
        {% if s.url %}<a href="{{ s.url }}">{{ s.name }}</a>{% else %}<a href="{{ root }}">{{ s.name }}</a> (this site){% endif %}
        {% if s.also_url %}<br><a href="{{ s.also_url }}">{{ s.also_label }}</a>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td><time datetime="{{ s.read_on.isoformat() }}">{{ s.read_on|date }}</time></td>
      <td>{{ s.covers }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.does_not_cover }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="counties">Counties</h2>
<p>
  The five counties with the most waters in Lake Notice's data on
  {{ as_of|date }} were {% for name, n in county_counts %}{{ name }} ({{ n }}){% if not loop.last %}{% if loop.revindex == 2 %} and {% else %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}.
  We list a county only where we read a page of its own. On {{ as_of|date }}
  we could not load the environmental health pages for
  {{ unread[:-1]|join(", ") }} and {{ unread[-1] }}, so this page says nothing about them.
</p>

<h2 id="levels">Why two pages can show different levels</h2>
<p>
  Sources cover different spots and different days. A water's headline on
  Lake Notice shows the highest level among its reported spots, so a page that
  covers only one swim area can show a lower level for the same lake. Each
  water page lists every spot and its latest status.
</p>

<h2 id="more">More</h2>
<p>
  <a href="{{ root }}about/">About the data and its limits</a> &middot;
  <a href="{{ root }}dogs/">Dogs and algae</a> &middot;
  <a href="{{ root }}county/">Find a lake by county</a>
</p>
{% endblock %}
